"""The bar: the table's configurations after local search. The search per instance, about four minutes: L-BFGS on
the hull volume of the directions (mv.maximize) from the published coordinates, two minutes of basin hopping
(mv.improve: shake all points or a point and its nearest neighbours by 1e-3 to 3e-1 of the edge length, maximize,
keep gains), a one-minute settle pass and a one-minute probe that was not kept. The table's configurations are already
at local maxima: the first ascent raised the volume by at most 4e-15 and the basin hopping found no other basin
above any of the 127, so the bar is the published configuration up to binary64 rounding (above it by at most 4.6e-15)
and beats no displayed volume. The probe after the bar gained at most 3.5e-16 (1.8e-16 relative). VOLUME is the
exact volume of the stored points as the evaluator computes it, as numerator/denominator; COORDS the points as base64
of little-endian binary64 rows."""

